{
    "name": "YeastVar1011",
    "biotoolsID": "yeastvar1011",
    "description": "A browser-based research-plan workbench for yeast single-cell studies, with searchable marker evidence, quality-control metrics, methods, input requirements, citations, and plan exports. Research modules cover cell states, expression variability, RNA dynamics, regulation, and population genetics. A separate Linux x86_64 Snakemake workflow performs FastQC, STARsolo tagged BAM and Gene/GeneFull/SJ/Velocyto matrix generation, samtools and per-barcode QC, and MultiQC for a known fixed single-segment CB/UMI layout with separate barcode and cDNA reads. SLURM execution requires a configured cluster profile. The browser does not execute sequencing analyses. Original code is MIT-licensed; third-party components and scientific sources retain their documented terms.",
